          "teacher_guidance": "Authoritative archival documentary capturing Justice Robert H. Jackson's opening address, the screening of liberating film evidence inside the courtroom, and the cross-examination of Hermann Göring and Nazi leadership. Recommended Watch Window: 02:00–10:30 • Lesson Phase: In-Depth Documentary Investigation & International Justice. Tone Alert: Solemn, historic judicial documentary featuring primary courtroom audio.",
          "viewing_task": "<ol><li><strong>[03:15] Recall:</strong> What famous warning did US Chief Prosecutor Robert H. Jackson deliver in his opening statement regarding the historical significance of the Nuremberg Trials?</li><li><strong>[06:40] Explain:</strong> How did Allied prosecutors use Nazi Germany's own captured administrative records, films, and government memos rather than eyewitness testimony as the bedrock of their prosecution?</li><li><strong>[09:20] Challenge:</strong> Evaluate whether the Nuremberg Trials successfully delivered justice: did executing key leaders heal the moral devastation of the Holocaust, and how did it establish the universal principle of individual criminal responsibility?</li></ol>",
          "model_answer": "<ol><li><strong>Recall:</strong> \"That four great nations, flushed with victory and stung with injury, stay the hand of vengeance and voluntarily submit their captive enemies to the judgment of the law is one of the most significant tributes that Power has ever paid to Reason.\"</li><li><strong>Explain:</strong> Jackson recognized that defendants might accuse eyewitnesses of emotional bias or exaggerating trauma. By relying on millions of pages of meticulous Nazi paperwork, typed transport manifests, minutes of the Wannsee Conference, and SS extermination reports, prosecutors proved that genocide was the deliberate policy of the Nazi state using the regime's own undeniable paperwork.</li><li><strong>Challenge:</strong> Executing a dozen Nazi leaders could never compensate for the slaughter of six million innocent people. However, Nuremberg succeeded in creating an incontrovertible evidentiary record that permanently discredited the Nazi regime and made Holocaust denial legally impossible. Crucially, it established that heads of state and military commanders cannot shield themselves behind sovereignty or \"following orders\", establishing the foundation for all modern international human rights law.</li></ol>"
