            "context": "When British troops entered Bergen-Belsen on 15 April 1945 under a localized truce arranged to contain a catastrophic typhus epidemic, they were confronted with human suffering on an unprecedented scale. British medical units worked tirelessly to establish emergency hospitals, but over 13,000 survivors died in the weeks following liberation due to severe malnutrition and disease. **Hinge Question:** Why was photographic and film documentation produced by Allied military units at Bergen-Belsen and Dachau in 1945 decisive in defeating Nazi wartime attempts to conceal the Holocaust?",
