            "citation": "United States Holocaust Memorial Museum (USHMM Photo Archives, Accession 1988.115.1) / Central Zionist Archives (Jerusalem, CZA-EXODUS-1947).",
            "context": "In the immediate aftermath of liberation, hundreds of thousands of surviving European Jews found themselves stateless displaced persons (DPs), unable or unwilling to return to homes and communities where anti-Semitic pogroms still erupted (such as the Kielce pogrom of July 1946). The plight of the SS Exodus passengers became an international symbol of the ongoing crisis of Jewish displacement. **Hinge Question:** Why did the plight of displaced Holocaust survivors between 1945 and 1948 accelerate international support for the United Nations Partition Plan for Palestine?",
